{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466488",
      "title": "Analyzing the AppModule",
      "lectureOrder": 647,
      "videoOrder": 595,
      "sourceHash": "4b70a5f9ed2153ff645248337e58fe9e6962b8cdbd1916c34f30e4e4361a622c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 3.39,
          "en": "Tutor: This is our project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.39,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "and there we have the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 7.83,
          "en": "Actually, this is not the only module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "and again, with module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "I mean things with that NgModule decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 14.61,
          "en": "we gather one other module in this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 16.65,
          "en": "and that would be the AppRoutingModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.65,
          "end": 19.377,
          "en": "Here, we also have @NgModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 24.3,
          "en": "So we already do use two modules and we use these modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 27.63,
          "en": "to set certain things up and group certain things together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.63,
          "end": 29.94,
          "en": "Now let's start with the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 33.51,
          "en": "There we have a long list of declarations, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.51,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "As I mentioned when we added things to that list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 39.84,
          "en": "declarations is in the end array of all the components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.84,
          "end": 43.02,
          "en": "directives, and custom pipes you're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.02,
          "end": 44.52,
          "en": "in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.52,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "So all these things have to go into declarations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "otherwise you can't use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "in your templates or in your routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 54.33,
          "en": "We also have that imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.33,
          "end": 56.94,
          "en": "The imports array here is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.94,
          "end": 60.21,
          "en": "because that allows you to import other modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.21,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "into this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "So the imports array here is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 67.14,
          "en": "to split your app into multiple modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.14,
          "end": 69.87,
          "en": "Thus far, we created only one extra module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 71.385,
          "en": "the AppRoutingModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.385,
          "end": 73.59,
          "en": "but we're using a couple of modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 73.59,
          "end": 76.104,
          "en": "that ship with Angular like the FormsModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.104,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "the ReactiveFormsModule, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "Now, if we were to look into such a module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 82.26,
          "en": "like the FormsModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 86.01,
          "en": "we would find a module with @NGModule as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 86.01,
          "end": 88.38,
          "en": "And in there we would have a declarations array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.38,
          "end": 91.8,
          "en": "with all the form related directives Angular supports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91.8,
          "end": 95.72999999999999,
          "en": "So things like automatically detecting a form element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 95.72999999999999,
          "end": 98.37,
          "en": "to create a form with the template driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.37,
          "end": 100.97999999999999,
          "en": "or the required, or the email directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.97999999999999,
          "end": 103.97999999999999,
          "en": "So all of that is basically included in the FormsModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.97999999999999,
          "end": 105.47999999999999,
          "en": "and so that you don't have to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 108.99000000000001,
          "en": "all these features individually to your declarations array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 108.99000000000001,
          "end": 112.293,
          "en": "we can simply import the FormsModule, which speeds this up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.34,
          "end": 116.94,
          "en": "The providers array here then is another important key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 118.28999999999999,
          "en": "in our NGModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "Here we define all the services we wanna provide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "however, I'll come back to services and modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 126.87,
          "en": "because that's kind of special.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.87,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "It's not the case that you can only use a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.06,
          "en": "in the module where you're provided,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.06,
          "end": 134.04,
          "en": "or at least that's not always the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.04,
          "end": 135.54,
          "en": "But I will come back to that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.54,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "for now it's important to know any service you plan",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 140.73,
          "en": "on injecting needs to be provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 140.73,
          "end": 143.4,
          "en": "and typically you do this in the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.4,
          "end": 148.4,
          "en": "or you do that by adding that providedIn root key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "into that object you pass to add injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 153.87,
          "en": "This is an alternative to adding that service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 153.87,
          "end": 156.36,
          "en": "to your AppModule providers array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 156.36,
          "end": 159.21,
          "en": "and this is actually the way I would use because it's faster",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 159.21,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "but you could also add a service here to providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 164.163,
          "en": "and it would also be available application wide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "Now, the bootstrap array is important for starting your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 172.77,
          "en": "It defines which component is available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "right in that index.html file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 178.17000000000002,
          "en": "And typically you only have one component there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.17000000000002,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "You could have multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 182.01,
          "en": "which is why bootstrap is also an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 182.01,
          "end": 183.81,
          "en": "you could define multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "but each component would then kind of be detached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 187.47,
          "en": "from the other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 191.43,
          "en": "You would be creating different root component trees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 191.43,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "in your application, and that is rarely what you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "because it makes working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.06,
          "en": "between these components way harder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 198.06,
          "end": 200.61,
          "en": "So therefore, you typically have one root component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.61,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "and you add that to the bootstrap array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 205.95,
          "en": "Well, and then we have the entryComponents here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 205.95,
          "end": 209.97,
          "en": "that simply is important for components you create in code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 209.97,
          "end": 213.09,
          "en": "as you learned in the sectional dynamic components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 213.09,
          "end": 216,
          "en": "this allows Angular to be aware of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 219.15,
          "en": "when it needs to create it programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 219.15,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned, we do have one other module right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "and that's the AppRoutingModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 225.84,
          "en": "which we also added to imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 225.84,
          "end": 228.42000000000002,
          "en": "The AppRoutingModule is simply there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 228.42000000000002,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "to hold our route configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "We could absolutely add this into our AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 238.02,
          "en": "we only outsourced it because it's quite a lot of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 238.02,
          "end": 241.08,
          "en": "and it keeps our AppModule a bit leaner,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 241.08,
          "end": 242.4,
          "en": "and that is already one reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 242.4,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "for why you might want to split your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 245.04,
          "end": 246.51,
          "en": "into multiple modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 246.51,
          "end": 249.21,
          "en": "It can make your existing modules leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 249.21,
          "end": 253.29,
          "en": "and more focused and easier to edit and to maintain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 255,
          "en": "Now, the AppRoutingModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 255,
          "end": 258.84,
          "en": "simply imports the RouterModule Angular offers us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 258.84,
          "end": 262.92,
          "en": "and uses a special method offered by that module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 262.92,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "which then takes our route configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "to configure the Angular/Router with our route config,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 270.78,
          "en": "and then something important happens;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 270.78,
          "end": 275.78,
          "en": "we export that RouterModule here from the AppRoutingModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 275.85,
          "end": 279.27,
          "en": "We need to do that because every module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 279.27,
          "end": 281.43,
          "en": "and now that is something you have to memorize,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 281.43,
          "end": 284.73,
          "en": "every module works on its own in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 284.73,
          "end": 286.95,
          "en": "They don't communicate with each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 286.95,
          "end": 290.07,
          "en": "If you declare a component in a certain component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 290.07,
          "end": 292.14,
          "en": "in a certain module, like AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 292.14,
          "end": 294.36,
          "en": "if we declare RecipesComponent here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 294.36,
          "end": 297.65999999999997,
          "en": "then we can only use it in here, nowhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "We can only use it in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 300.51,
          "en": "So we can use the selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 300.51,
          "end": 303.84,
          "en": "in our other components we declared here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 303.84,
          "end": 307.38,
          "en": "but if we would have another module with other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 309.6,
          "en": "then we could not use selectors of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 309.6,
          "end": 312.39,
          "en": "defined here in components of that other module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 312.39,
          "end": 314.52,
          "en": "and we'll see this in action very soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 314.52,
          "end": 317.73,
          "en": "And therefore here, we have to export the RouterModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 317.73,
          "end": 319.53,
          "en": "with our route configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 319.53,
          "end": 322.59,
          "en": "so that it really is not just available in this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 322.59,
          "end": 324.63,
          "en": "which would not be helpful at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 324.63,
          "end": 327.06,
          "en": "but that it is available in the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 327.06,
          "end": 329.4,
          "en": "where we now import AppRoutingModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 329.4,
          "end": 331.65,
          "en": "And when we import another module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 331.65,
          "end": 334.53,
          "en": "we import everything that module exports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 334.53,
          "end": 337.11,
          "en": "which in this case is our configured RouterModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 339.51,
          "en": "And this is how the configured RouterModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 339.51,
          "end": 342.75,
          "en": "ends up in the AppModule and is available there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 342.75,
          "end": 345.54,
          "en": "So that is generally what we're already doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 345.54,
          "end": 348.21,
          "en": "and what we're already using in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 348.21,
          "end": 351.65999999999997,
          "en": "We're using these modules and everything works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 351.65999999999997,
          "end": 354.15,
          "en": "Now for smaller applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 354.15,
          "end": 357.24,
          "en": "you can absolutely leave it that way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 357.24,
          "end": 358.59000000000003,
          "en": "Nothing wrong with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 358.59000000000003,
          "end": 361.08,
          "en": "This AppModule also is not too big.",
